  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development in Africa with Radio Astronomy Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Newton Fund builds research and innovation partnerships with developing countries across the world to promote the economic development and social welfare of the partner countries.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We will conduct a training programme in radio astronomy in Africa that will help to drive economic growth. South Africa is hosting part of the Square Kilometre Array (SKA) - the major next generation radio telescope and the first big science project on the African continent. The grant will
a)	Provide a basic training in the skills involved in radio astronomy to ten trainees per year in Ghana, Zambia, Kenya, Namibia/Botswana, Madagascar and Mozambique to enable them to use the radio antennas in these countries that will form the African VLBI Network (AVN). The advanced STEM skills they learn will also enable them to drive economic development in a variety of related industries such as telecommunications, space science, computing and big data. Their participation in this big science project in Africa will encourage more take up of advanced STEM subjects and subsequent economic development
b)	Provide advanced training in skills at MSc and PhD level to a number of students from AVN countries to enable them to carry out research using the AVN. These students will be able to form the foundation of radio astronomy groups in their countries. 
c)	Build a sustainable network of African radio astronomers who can collaborate with each other and utilize the AVN. They will also build links with both UK and SA experts in the fields of radio astronomy and related industrial fields that will lead to a sustainable collaborative network. 
d)	Construct a virtual centre of excellence that will act as a repository for training materials, a contact database for academics and industrial partners, a platform for further opportunities, and a place for entrepreneurs and business ideas to develop.</narrative>
  </description>
